{"kind":"request","text":"Bound resident memory so a 500,000-record workroom fits the FIRST-PRODUCTION envelope.","body":{"conditions":"Measured at main adda28c8 (docs/reference/performance.md): warm resident peak RSS is 135 MB at depth 5,000, 937 MB at 50,000 and 9,183 MB at 500,000, a slope of about 17.8 KB per record. The memory work merged as 5fc9929c roughly halved the previous slope and brought PREVIEW inside its 1 GiB target at 937 MB, about 12 percent of headroom, so PREVIEW passes. FIRST-PRODUCTION still needs 9.18 GB against a 4 GiB target and is a direct measurement, not a projection: the 500,000-record figure was observed on a fixture, not extrapolated. Suspected bounding component: the linear-history projection retains every application event in memory, so residency is linear in depth with no eviction or paging. Satisfied when a resident serving 500,000 records stays under 4 GiB peak RSS, with the per-record slope re-measured and reported at 5,000, 50,000 and 500,000, and without weakening what the projection can answer.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}